course: dictionary
lesson: 14022
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and maintain is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning is in use. «Dad maintains his bike by oiling the chain.» Here maintain means looking after something so it stays in good condition.
explain: «The runner maintained a speed of 10 km/h for the whole race.» Maintain means keeping something at the same level. The speed did not go up or down. Try the swap: "kept a speed of 10 km/h" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Ruby maintained that the answer was 12, even when everyone disagreed.» Here maintain means saying firmly that something is true. The clues are "even when everyone disagreed". Ask yourself: what word would fit here? "Kept saying" would fit, so that is the meaning.
fact: Maintain is a verb, so it shows an action: maintain, maintains, maintained, maintaining.
fact: «Maintain» can mean to look after something so it stays in good condition, like a bike or a garden.
fact: «Maintain» can mean to keep something at the same level, such as a speed or a temperature.
fact: «Maintain» can mean to keep saying something is true, even when others disagree.
fact: In science, «maintain a constant temperature» keeps a test fair, because only one thing is allowed to change.
exercise: «Sam maintains his garden every weekend.» What does maintains mean here? | Sells it to a neighbour | *Looks after it to keep it in good condition | Forgets that it exists | Paints it bright red
exercise: «The car maintained 50 km/h on the motorway.» What does this tell us? | The car went backwards | The car got faster and faster | *The speed stayed the same | The car stopped suddenly
exercise: «Ella maintained that the moon is made of cheese.» What does maintained mean here? | Whispered it quietly | Proved it with a test | *Kept saying firmly that it was true | Forgot all about it
test: «Mum maintained that dinner would be at six, even when we begged.» What does maintained mean? | *Kept saying firmly | Changed her mind | Shouted loudly | Asked a question
test: «The machine must maintain a constant temperature to keep the test fair.» What does maintain mean? | *Keep at the same level | Switch it off | Measure the time it takes | Make it hotter every minute
exam: «The council pays to maintain the park and the swings.» Which meaning fits best? | *Keep them in good condition by looking after them | Build a brand new park from scratch | Paint them all blue | Get rid of them completely
